WEBVTT

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.790
Woody and Forky were last seen
on the highway.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.470
But where is the highway?

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.870
VOICE BOX: The slingshot
maneuver is all we've got!

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.430
Full speed ahead!

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.710
(PEOPLE EXCLAIMING)

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.630
Thanks, inner voice!

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.710
(WOMAN WHOOPING)

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.270
Hi-ya!

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.550
The highway.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.710
On my way, Woody!

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.030
(GASPS)

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.990
(GROANS)

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:45.990
(EXCLAIMS)

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.350
Rad.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.150
AXEL: Hey! Step right up!

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.310
Put your money down!

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.430
Get yourself
a real Buzz Lightyear!

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.030
Hey! Hey!

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.310
(METAL CREAKING)

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:06.670
Harmony, honey. Sunscreen.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:07.830
Okay.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.070
Be right back, Mr. Cowboy.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.070
(PANTING)

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.990
Okay. Antique store,
antique store...

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:22.190
Oh, that way!

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:26.950
(GRUNTING)

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:34.790
(EXCLAIMS)

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.510
(CHILDREN CHATTERING
EXCITEDLY)

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.830
Did you see 'em?
How many are there?

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.150
-WOODY: Whoa, whoa.
-We got a busload of campers!

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.190
-(TOYS GRUNTING)
-COMBAT CARL: Here they come!

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.590
WOODY: Huh?
COMBAT CARL: Playtime, baby!

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.390
(RUMBLING)

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:52.670
(CHILDREN CHATTERING)

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.110
(KID WHOOPING)

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.030
(BOY GASPS)

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.950
Oh, baby!
It's a good day to play, huh?

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.270
Am I right? (LAUGHS)

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.750
(SHEEP BLEATING)

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:09.670
Huh?

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.230
(GASPS)

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.670
LISA: "Hello, Mr. Cowboy.
How are you today?

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.670
"Do you like riding horses?"

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.230
BETH: Wanna play
on the swings?

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.550
LISA: Wait for me!

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.190
-Bo?
-(GIRLS GIGGLING)

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.350
Come on.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:48.870
(WOODY YELLS, GRUNTS)

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:50.670
Bo!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.150
(LAUGHS) Oh, I can't
believe it's you!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.670
Bo Peep!

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.350
I never thought
I'd see you again!

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.430
(BOTH CHUCKLE AWKWARDLY)

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.590
-So, which kid is yours?
-WOODY: Which one is yours?

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.830
-BO PEEP: None.
-No one.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.030
-Wait, you're a lost toy?
-You're a lost toy?

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.390
-That's awful.
-That's great.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.150
-Huh?
-I mean, awfully great...

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.070
-that you are lost out here.
-(RUSTLING)

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.230
-(GASPS) Skunk, skunk, skunk!
-BO PEEP: Watch out!

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.350
-(YELPS) Huh?
-(WHIRRING)

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:20.910
I told you
not to drive so fast.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.310
You almost ran him over.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.270
(BLEATING)

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.510
Oh, hey, guys!

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:26.870
(LAUGHS) Whoa! Hold on there!

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.830
Okay!
I missed you, too.

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:31.910
If it isn't Bobby?
Gus?

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.070
Uh...

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.230
Lefty?

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.510
Billy, Goat, and Gruff.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.350
Right! Right! Right!
Sorry, guys.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:39.190
-BO PEEP: Girls.
-Girls! Of course!

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.390
(BLEATING)

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.390
BO PEEP: All right, all right.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:44.710
Okay, let's get a look at you.
You need any repairs?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.870
-Repairs? No, I'm fine.
-(BLEATING)

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.030
Hey! Nice find, girls.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.270
Where did you get
all this stuff?

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:51.350
Here and there.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.190
You know, some kids
play rougher than others...

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:55.950
(CHUCKLES) so I try
to be prepared.

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:57.590
How long have you been
out on your own?

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.470
Seven fantastic years!

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:00.630
Seven?

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.110
You would not believe
the things I've seen.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.470
-(BLEATING)
-Uh, no.

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:05.670
-Gigs.
-GIGGLE: Yo!

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.710
Come on out. There's someone
I want you to meet.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.310
Be right down.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.190
What's the situation?
We heading out of town or...

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:17.590
Whoa! Who's this?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.430
You remember the rag doll
I told you about?

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.710
-The cowboy?
-Yep!

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.550
No way! (LAUGHS)

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.870
BO PEEP: Don't stare.
GIGGLE: I'm totally staring.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:29.550
Woody,
this is Giggle McDimples.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:30.910
(GIGGLES)

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:31.990
Oh, hi, Giggle.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.950
Whoa, you didn't tell me
he was a cop.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.270
Howdy, Sheriff.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.910
Officer Giggle McDimples.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.830
I run Pet Patrol
for Mini-Opolis.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.030
Yeah, search and rescue.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:41.190
Ants, caterpillars,

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.830
-miniature poodles, spiders.
-COMBAT CARL: Hut! Hut! Hut!

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.590
Carl! Where you headed?

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.390
Combat Carl just heard
there's a birthday party...

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.990
at the playground
on Main Street.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.750
Rumor has it
they got two piñatas.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.190
-That could be 20 to 30 kids.
-Nice!

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.110
Oh, yeah! Combat Carl's
gettin' played with!

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:56.750
You guys in?

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.430
You bet! Woody,
you are gonna love this!

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.390
Uh, no, I can't, sir.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.230
Bo, I need to get back
to my kid.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:04.950
-ALL: What?
-You got a kid?

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.110
Yeah.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.590
COMBAT CARL: Way to beat
the odds, soldier.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.790
Meet you
at the playground, Peep.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.510
Combat Carl's got
a piñata party to crash.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.870
All right, move out.
Hut! Hut! Hut!

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:18.470
So, you're, uh, with a kid?

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:19.670
It's not Andy, is it?

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.750
No, no, no.
He went off to college.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.710
But he gave us to Bonnie.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.710
-You have a little girl?
-No way!

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:27.310
Yeah, yeah.
It's why I'm out here.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.750
Her other toy is trapped

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:29.990
in this antique store,
and I have to...

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.830
Second Chance Antiques?

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.270
We know that store.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.830
That's great. That is great!

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.550
If you know the store,
you could really

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.830
-help me find him...
-No way.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:39.030
We wasted years there,

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.550
just sitting on the shelf,
collecting dust.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.190
Oh, Bo, that's awful.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.430
But I don't have a choice.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.230
I have to get that toy
from Gabby.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.990
Whoa. Steer clear
of that weirdo.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.390
If I were you, I'd cut
my losses and go home.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.590
But Bonnie needs him
to get through kindergarten.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.990
Kids lose toys every day.
Bonnie will get over it.

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:55.670
No, no...

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:59.350
You see, Bonnie needs him
just like Molly needed you.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:00.910
(BLEATING EXCITEDLY)

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.310
Aw, no. Sorry, girls.

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:03.790
-Molly's not here.
-(BLEATS WEAKLY)

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.790
GIGGLE: Molly? Bo,
I didn't know you had a kid.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:07.790
That was a long time ago.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.070
Oh, Bo's kid was
something special.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.870
She was the cutest thing...

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.670
but so afraid of the dark.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.430
It was just a phase.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:16.870
Oh, you weren't there
in the beginning.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:18.950
Hearing Molly cry
each night...

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.270
it broke every toy's heart.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:24.710
And then,
Bo came into the room.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.670
Her lamp was the only thing
that made Molly feel safe.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:30.870
Mom would let her keep Bo on
all night.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.830
Ha! Who knew you were
such a softy?

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.230
And Molly would fall asleep

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.390
with her hand
resting on Bo's feet.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.750
-Okay! Okay. I get it.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.670
Bo, my kid really needs
this toy.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:46.470
Will you help me?
For old times' sake.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:47.910
(SIGHS)

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:49.710
All right, all right.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.470
-Thank you! Oh!
-(BO PEEP LAUGHS)

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:52.670
-Oh, thank you!
-All right.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:54.590
Guess we're doing this.
Let's ride!

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.150
(BLEATING)

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:00.110
Second Chance Antiques,
and step on it.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.350
(BLEATING)

